-- title:
--   Primitive qℓ-th root of unity on each component
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\ne q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with finite residue field whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$. Assume: the variable-change stability of level-$\ell$ data, i.e. whenever $D$ is a [`ModularCurve.LevelPData`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L43) over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ satisfying `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ D` then `D.variableChange C` satisfies it for $C\bullet W$; the analogous stability of the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` under $C$ and `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, which is chord-and-tangent (its points are identified, additively and Galois-equivariantly, with the affine points after base change to fields) and whose unit section is the origin of the chart at infinity; a transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes, whose sections are compatible with the graded homomorphisms of the projective models (`IsSectionTransport`); and the existence of such graded homomorphisms realising variable changes (`hVC`) and coefficient maps (`hCO`), each dominating the irrelevant ideal. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the moduli problem `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, whose points over $T$ are variable-change orbits of tuples consisting of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant, a $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-type kernel polynomial for each prime $p\mid M'$, a level-$\ell$ structure, and a Drinfeld basis of the $q$-torsion; suppose its coordinate ring $P_0.B_0$ is a finite-type $A_0$-algebra, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a minimal prime of $P_0.B_0$. Then some $b\in P_0.B_0$ has image in $P_0.B_0/\mathfrak P$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity.
--
--   This is the assertion, in the style of Katz–Mazur's analysis of the fine moduli schemes of full level structures, that each irreducible component of the moduli ring over an unramified base of residue characteristic $q$ carries primitive $q\ell$-th roots of unity, obtained from the Weil pairings of the level-$q$ Drinfeld basis and of the level-$\ell$ structure. It feeds the classification of $A_0$-algebra maps out of the moduli ring and the unramifiedness statements for the completions of its components.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_isPrimitiveRoot_quotient_mk_of_mem_minimalPrimes_levelModuliPackageAbs_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_natCast_gamma0Pow.lean

